<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="info-updated">Last updated: <%= updated %></p>

<p>Atlasphere helps groups of friends plan trips together. This policy explains what we collect, why, who we share it with, and the choices you have. It covers the website and the Atlasphere mobile app.</p>

<h2>What we collect</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Account details:</strong> your name, email address, phone number, and, if you choose to give it, your gender. Your password is stored only as a secure hash.</li>
  <li><strong>Profile:</strong> your profile photo, and the countries and cities you mark as visited.</li>
  <li><strong>Trips:</strong> the trips you create or join, messages you send in trip chats, your votes on activities, itinerary plans and notes.</li>
  <li><strong>Friends:</strong> friend requests you send, accept or decline.</li>
  <li><strong>Technical:</strong> a sign-in cookie that keeps you logged in (for 7 days), your light/dark theme choice saved in your browser, and the server logs our host keeps, which include IP addresses. The mobile app keeps your sign-in token in your phone’s secure storage.</li>
</ul>
<p>We don’t use advertising or analytics trackers, and we don’t use your device’s location.</p>

<h2>How we use it</h2>
<ul>
  <li>To run your account and sign you in, including sending verification codes and password-reset emails.</li>
  <li>To let you plan trips with the people in them: they see your name, photo, messages, votes and plans in that trip.</li>
  <li>To show your profile: friends see your visited places and planned trips; everyone else sees only your name, photo and friend count.</li>
  <li>To notify you about trip activity and friend requests.</li>
</ul>
<p>We don’t sell your data.</p>

<h2>Services we rely on</h2>
<p>Some of your data is processed by these providers on our behalf:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Railway</strong>: hosts the app and stores uploaded photos.</li>
  <li><strong>Aiven</strong>: hosts the database.</li>
  <li><strong>Brevo</strong>: sends emails (your email address and the message).</li>
</ul>
<p>To show recommendations, weather and maps, our server sends destination names or coordinates (never your personal details) to Geoapify, Pexels, Open-Meteo, MET Norway and Nager.Date. Map images load in your browser from OpenStreetMap, which sees your IP address like any website you visit.</p>

<h2>Deleting your data</h2>
<p>You can delete your account in <a href="/settings">Settings</a> › Delete Account. This removes your account, profile and friendships. Messages you sent in trip chats stay in those chats so the conversation still makes sense for the others. To have those or anything else removed, email us and we’ll do it.</p>

<h2>Your rights</h2>
<p>You can ask us for a copy of your data, to correct it, or to delete it, by emailing <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a>. If you’re in the EU or UK you also have the right to complain to your data protection authority.</p>

<h2>Children</h2>
<p>Atlasphere isn’t meant for children under 16.</p>

<h2>Changes</h2>
<p>If we change this policy we’ll update the date above, and tell you in the app for important changes.</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>Questions? Email <a href="mailto:<%= supportEmail %>"><%= supportEmail %></a>.</p>
